d yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Utah remains one of the most Republican states on the presidential map, and the open-seat contest to succeed the term-limited president starts with that structural advantage on the Republican side. No public polls of the state are available and no expert ratings have been issued, so the outlook rests on partisanship and fundamentals. Recent reporting suggests a difficult national climate for the president's party, with approval positive in only a handful of states, but Utah coverage finds would-be Trump successors rating higher among Utahns than the president, cushioning the Republican position.\n\nThe state's Republican lean points to a comfortable but not overwhelming Republican win. Opinion commentary asks whether Utah is trending blue, but a statewide presidential victory would require a far larger shift than current evidence shows. Uncertainty is wide in the absence of polling, and the margin could move once nominees and campaigns take shape.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1067, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1478, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1592, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1542, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1457, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1497, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1506, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1453, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1504, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1517, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1576, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.131, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.156, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1532, "margin": -11